															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/mew-ltiverse" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5271378); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5271378&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607200972" alt="Mew-ltiverse" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5271378)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/mew-ltiverse" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5271378); return false;" >Mew-ltiverse</a></span> <span class="odate time_1569085535 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">21 Sep 2019 17:05</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4371114">
									

<p>Floppy was a joy to work with! She was very patient and our ideas worked very well together. ^^</p>
<p>So I was searching through the wikimedia commons a few months back and found this picture. I showed it to the team bird members, and <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/not-a-seagull" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3009022); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3009022&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1569085535" alt="not_a_seagull" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3009022)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/not-a-seagull" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3009022); return false;">not_a_seagull</a></span> helped me brainstorm for it. Months passed, and I never did anything with it.</p>
<p>I asked Floppy recently if she wanted to collab, and she said yes! A few weeks later we began brainstorming, and I brought up the idea Seagull had helped me with. Floppy suggested some changes that we both liked, and we got to work!</p>
<p>This piece means a lot to me because I wrote a lot of the dialogue, the first two interviews (floppy tweaked the second one by adding some things that only made it better!) and I helped characterize Goshawk and created Nour, which were important later on. Anyone who knows me, knows I’m <em>abysmal</em> with dialogue. But the fact that I was able to write good dialogue on pretty much first try means a lot to me. And, I love what Flopoy did with Nour and Goshawk later on!</p>
<p>Idk I ramble, but thanks to Floppy so much for working with me!</p>
<p>And of course, thanks to those who crit this. ^^</p>

